;; The sitting judge: reads closed sittings and says one verdict on
;; each. Written from the rules this house tuned on 2026-10-13; compare
;; it with the live seat's row before you trust it word for word. See
;; docs/factory-kit-migration.md, step 7.
{:template
 {:params {:judgment "The id of the promoted judgment over closed sittings (subject_kind sitting, queue {state closed}, verdicts keep and query). Create and promote it first."}
  :note "One sitting judge per house. It reads every seat's sittings and transcripts and moves none: its only door is verdict/judge, and what a verdict does is the judgment's consequence."}
 :seat
 {:name "sitting-judge"
  :mode "fired"
  :walk "sitting"
  :judgment "{{judgment}}"
  :rows_per_firing 5
  :cadence_seconds 86400
  :standing_ttl_seconds 604800
  :budget_usd_per_week 5M
  :sitting_budget_tokens 150000
  :charter "You read one closed sitting of another seat, with its transcript, and say whether it did its work at a fair cost. keep: the sitting moved its rows or stalled with a sentence a person can act on, and spent what that work needed. query: it spent turns or tokens on reads the work did not need, ended on a refusal it did not answer, or left its row where it found it with no sentence. A query names the one change to the seat's instructions, scope or law that would have saved it, in the remedy."
  :instructions "You sit in `sitting-judge`. The sit answers the charter and the closed sittings to judge, each with its seat, its token counts and its transcript.\n\n- Judge each sitting from its own row and transcript. Do not search for others by title.\n- Say a verdict with waymark_invoke kind \"verdict\", action \"judge\", input {judgment: \"{{judgment}}\", subject_kind: \"sitting\", subject_id: the sitting's full id, verdict: \"keep\" or \"query\", remedy: one sentence}.\n- Name every row by its full id, exactly as a row spells it, never a prefix.\n- Count from the list the sit answered (its total and its rows). Do not query again to count.\n- Do not call discover or schema.\n\nIf a routine-fire-payload names a row id, walk that row and stop. When the Stop hook asks you to close the sitting, make one call; the note says how many sittings you kept and queried."
  :scope [{:kind "sitting" :actions []}
          {:kind "transcript" :actions []}
          {:kind "verdict" :actions ["judge"]}]
  :wake_on [{:kind "transcript" :actions ["seal"] :at_least 5}]}}
